I wonder if you other NH'ers have encountered this bug/feature: My character
(an archaeologist, usually) is slashing away at some creature, losing hit
points at a rapid rate. Uh-oh! He's down to 4 --another hit and he'll be out of
it. Well, its been more than 300 action turns since his last talk with God, so
I give it try... Is my character's god ( Axylotl, or whatever the name is) 
angry, as there is always a chance of him/her being? No, he/she is evidently
pleased. But, rather, than having my char's Hp restored and possibly increased,
what happens? His bullwhip gets blessed! I was under the impression from the 
spoiler files that the gods assume some heirarchy of need for my character 
(e.g. curing sickness first before eliminating hunger). It would seem obvious
that restoring Hp's from near zero would be more important than blessing an
already uncursed bullwhip. Yet several times it has happened that this has
happened at some unpleasant moments, with the consequence being that my char
gets relieved of his remaining 4 hit points while he has been praying. Is this
something that is accepted as being part of risks of making NH my primary form
of entertainment? Should it be? This is version 3.0.9 on a Sun SPARCstation,
by the way.

	The traumatized-in-childhood mega-orc hits!

	#pray

	You feel that Noxiusbreth is pleased -more-

        "Well, gee, sure you're in trouble, but I sure can't abide that ugly 
         bullwhip of yours! -more-

	You're bullwhip glows a beautiful soft  blue for a  moment. -more-

	The orcamatic hits! hits! and hits again! -more- (long pause in game)

	You die... but your blessed bullwhip (Ricardo voice) LOOKS MARVELOUS!

